.el .ds Aq '
.TH sway-things-record 1 "" "Sway Things 0.4.0" "Sway Things Manual"
.SH NAME
sway\-things\-record \- Start a recording of the screen with wf\-recorder or wl\-screenrec, or stop the one that runs so its file is complete; the recording key runs this
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsway\-things record\fR [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIAREA\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Start a recording of the screen with wf\-recorder or wl\-screenrec, or stop the one that runs so its file is complete; the recording key runs this
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Controls when to use color
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIAREA\fR]
What to record; without it, what the Screenshots & Clipboard page says
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
region: A region you select, or a window you click
.IP \(bu 2
display: The display with the focus
.RE
